TOPIC 4 : AGILE USER STORIES
======================================================================

Q1. What is a User Story, and why is it used in Agile?

Interview Ready Answer

A User Story is a short, simple description of a feature written from
the end user's perspective. It captures a user's requirement and
explains the value the feature provides. User Stories help the Scrum
Team understand customer needs and deliver business value
incrementally.

Definition

A User Story is a user-centric requirement written in simple language.

Purpose

• Capture customer requirements.
• Focus on user value.
• Help the Development Team understand business needs.
• Deliver features incrementally.

======================================================================

Q2. What is the standard format of a User Story?

Interview Ready Answer

The standard User Story format is:

As a <User>,
I want <Feature/Goal>,
So that <Benefit>.

Example

As a Student,

I want to upload my resume,

So that I can apply for placement opportunities.

Purpose

• Identify the user.
• Describe the required feature.
• Explain the business value.

======================================================================

Q3. What is the INVEST principle?

Interview Ready Answer

The INVEST principle is a checklist used to determine whether a User
Story is well-written and of high quality.

INVEST

I → Independent
N → Negotiable
V → Valuable
E → Estimable
S → Small
T → Testable

Purpose

• Improve User Story quality.
• Make estimation easier.
• Ensure stories are testable.
• Keep stories manageable within a Sprint.

======================================================================

Q4. What are Acceptance Criteria, and why is the Given–When–Then format
used?

Interview Ready Answer

Acceptance Criteria are the conditions that a User Story must satisfy
before it can be accepted as complete. They ensure the feature meets
business and customer requirements.

The Given–When–Then format makes Acceptance Criteria clear, testable,
and unambiguous.

Given
Initial condition or precondition.

When
Action performed by the user.

Then
Expected outcome.

Example

Given
The user is logged in.

When
The user clicks the Logout button.

Then
The user should be logged out successfully.

Purpose

• Define completion conditions.
• Remove ambiguity.
• Help testing.
• Ensure expected behavior.

======================================================================

Q5. Write a User Story and Acceptance Criteria for a feature.

Interview Ready Answer

User Story

As a user,

I want to reset my password,

So that I can regain access to my account if I forget it.

Acceptance Criteria

Given
The user is on the Forgot Password page.

When
The user enters a registered email address and clicks "Send OTP".

Then
The system should send an OTP to the registered email and allow the
user to reset the password after successful OTP verification.

