INTERVIEW TRAP QUESTIONS
======================================================================

Q1. Who writes User Stories?

Answer:
Generally, the Product Owner creates and maintains User Stories with
input from stakeholders and the Scrum Team.

------------------------------------------------------------

Q2. Is a User Story the same as Acceptance Criteria?

Answer:
No.

User Story → Describes what the user wants.

Acceptance Criteria → Define when the User Story is considered complete.

------------------------------------------------------------

Q3. Does INVEST stand for the Sprint process?

Answer:
No.

INVEST is a checklist for writing good User Stories.

------------------------------------------------------------

Q4. Is Given–When–Then mandatory?

Answer:
No.

It is a widely used and recommended format because it makes Acceptance
Criteria easy to understand and test.

------------------------------------------------------------

Q5. Can a User Story be marked as Done if one Acceptance Criterion
fails?

Answer:
No.

A User Story is considered complete only when all Acceptance Criteria
and the Definition of Done are satisfied.

